WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.767
Practice 1 reshapes student grades.

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:07.102
The source is long: one student-course grade per row.

00:00:07.102 --> 00:00:11.792
The output should have one row per student and fixed course columns.

00:00:11.792 --> 00:00:18.417
A missing course should remain NULL because no recorded grade is not the same as a grade of

00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:22.572
zero. For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:22.572 --> 00:00:27.697
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:27.697 --> 00:00:31.452
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:31.452 --> 00:00:36.102
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:43.127
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:43.127 --> 00:00:47.022
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project:

00:00:47.022 --> 00:00:51.476
validate the meaning of the result, not only whether the statement executes.
